# An allowlist: everything is out of the build context, and only what the image
# is built from comes back in. A deny list would let the next environment file,
# key, or state directory into the context by simply being new.
*
!pyproject.toml
!uv.lock
!src
!frontend

# What the build makes for itself, so a stale local copy never enters the context.
frontend/node_modules
frontend/.svelte-kit
src/hopin/web/build

**/__pycache__

# The tree above is admitted whole, so what must never be in an image is named
# again here: a secret or a key nested inside it would otherwise ride in on its
# parent directory.
**/.env*
**/*.pem
**/*.key
**/id_*
